    "result": "Perfect! The bug has been fixed. Here's a summary of what was wrong and what I changed:\n\n## The Bug\nWhen running `frai gate init --ci`, the `--ci` flag wasn't being passed through from the `frai` CLI to the underlying `frai-gate` CLI. This meant the workflow file `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` wasn't being created, even though the `FRAI-SPEC.md` file was.\n\n## The Root Cause\nThe gate command in `frai-cli/src/index.ts` (line 753) was using Commander.js's action handler with only the positional arguments (`args`), but unknown options like `--ci` were being consumed by Commander's parser and not included in the `args` array passed to the action handler.\n\n## The Fix\nI modified the gate command's action handler to extract all arguments (both positional and flags) directly from `process.argv` after the `gate` command, ensuring all flags are passed through to the `frai-gate` CLI:\n\n**Changed in `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-755):**\n- Added logic to find the 'gate' command in `process.argv`\n- Extract all remaining arguments after 'gate' using `process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1)`\n- Pass the complete argument list to `spawnSync`\n\nThe fix ensures that when running `frai gate init --ci`, all flags are correctly forwarded to the `frai-gate` CLI, which then properly creates both the spec file and the GitHub Actions workflow.\n\n\u2705 **Verification:** Ran the command and confirmed that both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created when using the `--ci` flag.",
